cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the archived release."
title: >-
  Readout choice, not model choice, determines whether pretrained genomic
  language models help: a pre-registered benchmark on fine-scale 16S rRNA
  discrimination
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, pre-registered plans, derived data and manuscript materials
  for a benchmark comparing four pretrained genomic language models
  (DNABERT-2, DNABERT-S, HyenaDNA, Nucleotide Transformer v2) against k-mer
  counting on target-versus-neighbour discrimination within single 16S rRNA
  hypervariable regions, across 58 analysable bacterial groups in three
  experiments with a locked confirmatory test set.
